# Security response headers for the Cloudflare Pages deployment.
# Cloudflare serves this file verbatim (it is copied from public/ into dist/ at build).
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# CSP notes (validated against the production build, 2026-06-30):
#   - script-src 'self'      — the Vite build emits only external module chunks from our origin;
#                              there are no inline <script> tags, so no hash/unsafe-inline is needed.
#   - style-src 'unsafe-inline' — the theming layer is an inline-style-object model, and the
#                              Google Fonts stylesheet is loaded from fonts.googleapis.com.
#   - connect-src ...supabase.co — Supabase REST (https) + Realtime (wss).
#   - img-src data:          — Vite may inline small SVG assets as data: URIs.
# If the Cloudflare preview deploy shows CSP violations in the console, relax the offending
# directive (or switch to Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only to observe first).

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'

# The service worker runs under this file's CSP, and it fetch()es Google Fonts to cache them —
# governed by connect-src, not font-src. Intent: scope that widening to the worker's own response
# path instead of the site-wide directive, since only sw.js needs it. Both hosts are already
# trusted for style-src/font-src above, so nothing new enters the trust set either way.
#
# NOT YET CONFIRMED: it is unverified whether Cloudflare Pages emits both matching header rules
# (the site-wide block above and this one) or has this one replace the other for a /sw.js request.
# If Pages emits both, browsers enforce the *intersection* of two same-name directives, which
# would silently drop the font hosts from connect-src for sw.js — the worker's fetch() for the
# Google Fonts stylesheet would then be CSP-blocked, and because cacheFirst has no network-failure
# fallback, that fails the stylesheet for every controlled page. Check a Cloudflare Pages preview
# deploy with the worker active: look for a connect-src violation in the console naming
# fonts.googleapis.com. If it fails, widen the site-wide connect-src directive above instead (and
# record why here) rather than relying on this scoped block.
/sw.js
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://fonts.googleapis.com https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
